Provenance
----------
Rashid is an independent, clean-room implementation. It contains no Apple
code and is not derived from Apple's Rosetta translation software. The
instruction decoder is written from the Intel Software Developer's Manual,
the loader from the public <mach-o/loader.h> headers, and the calling
convention conversion from the published System V x86-64 and AAPCS64 ABI
documents. See CONTRIBUTING.md for the contribution policy that keeps this
provenance defensible.

